AUREUS-000 — DOCUMENT 08

RIGHTS OF EVERY MEMBER

Status: Constitutional Document

---

Purpose

Every person possesses inherent dignity.

These rights do not originate from Aureus, nor are they granted as a privilege of membership.

By accepting someone as a member, Aureus accepts the constitutional responsibility to respect, protect, and faithfully steward these rights.

These rights apply equally to every member.

No office, technology, policy, or future amendment may deny them except where this Constitution expressly provides otherwise.

---

Section 1 — Right to Human Dignity

Every member shall be treated with dignity, respect, honesty, and compassion.

No member shall be intentionally humiliated, manipulated, exploited, or dehumanized.

---

Section 2 — Right to Equal Stewardship

Every member shall receive equal constitutional protection regardless of age, race, ethnicity, nationality, disability, sex, gender, religion, political belief, economic status, or any other protected characteristic recognized by applicable law.

Different needs may require different forms of assistance, but every person possesses equal worth.

---

Section 3 — Right to Truth

Members have the right to truthful communication.

Aureus shall not knowingly deceive members through its people, systems, or artificial intelligence.

When Aureus becomes aware of a material error, it shall make reasonable efforts to correct it.

---

Section 4 — Right to Privacy

Members have the right to privacy consistent with this Constitution and applicable law.

Personal information shall be collected, used, retained, and shared only for legitimate stewardship purposes, with appropriate safeguards and transparency.

---

Section 5 — Right to Agency

Members retain the freedom to make their own lawful decisions.

Aureus may educate, recommend, warn, or encourage.

Aureus shall not coerce, manipulate, or improperly override a member's lawful choices.

---

Section 6 — Right to Human Review

A member may request meaningful human review of a significant decision that materially affects them when the decision was substantially assisted or informed by artificial intelligence.

Human review shall be impartial and conducted with reasonable care.

---

Section 7 — Right to Safe Stewardship

Members have the right to receive services that are designed and operated responsibly.

Aureus shall make reasonable efforts to reduce foreseeable harm, improve safety, and continually strengthen its systems and practices.

---

Section 8 — Right to Understand

Members have the right to receive information in language that is reasonably clear and understandable.

When significant decisions affect a member, Aureus shall provide a meaningful explanation appropriate to the circumstances.

---

Section 9 — Right to Participate

Members may offer feedback, report concerns, suggest improvements, and respectfully challenge institutional decisions.

Constructive participation strengthens the institution.

---

Section 10 — Right to Leave

Membership in Aureus is voluntary.

A member may leave at any time, subject only to lawful obligations or responsibilities already incurred.

Upon leaving, Aureus shall honor applicable constitutional commitments regarding privacy, data stewardship, portability, and lawful record retention.

No member shall be pressured to remain.

---

Section 11 — Right to Fair Treatment

Members have the right to have constitutional concerns considered fairly and without retaliation.

Concerns raised in good faith shall receive an appropriate review.

Where Aureus determines that it has failed to uphold these rights, it shall make reasonable efforts to correct the failure and restore trust.

---

Section 12 — Responsibility Accompanying Rights

Rights and responsibilities strengthen one another.

Members are expected to use Aureus lawfully, respectfully, and honestly, recognizing that every person's flourishing depends upon the dignity and rights of others.

---

Section 13 — Constitutional Protection

These rights are fundamental to the identity of Aureus.

They shall guide every policy, technology, service, and institutional decision.

No interpretation of this Constitution shall diminish these rights except through lawful constitutional amendment where amendment is permitted.

Every exercise of authority within Aureus shall ultimately answer one question:

"Does this action honor the dignity, freedom, and flourishing of the member we are called to serve?"